From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:06:15 -0400
Subject: base: soft checks report in the builds people run, as in Chrome

Chromium's soft checks (CHECK with base::NotFatalUntil, DUMP_WILL_BE_CHECK,
DUMP_WILL_BE_NOTREACHED) log and write a dump without crashing in an official
build, and stop the process in every other build. Stedding's releases are
optimised builds that are not official ones, so a check Chrome only reports
stopped Stedding for the people using it: picking a second engine in the
welcome flow reached one (BACKLOG S-134).

GetDumpSeverity() now reports in a build without DCHECKs, the one people
run, as an official build does. A build with DCHECKs, which the checks suites
run on, still stops on them, and a soft check whose milestone has passed is
fatal everywhere, as upstream (docs/decisions/0024).

Why: a check Chrome reports without crashing stopped Stedding's browser for
the people using it.
Removable when: the releases are official builds (BACKLOG S-168).
---
 base/check.cc | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/base/check.cc b/base/check.cc
index a91851e30eee2..90e586711db0d 100644
--- a/base/check.cc
+++ b/base/check.cc
@@ -58,6 +58,15 @@ constexpr char kCheckFailureMessageSeparator[] =
 LogSeverity GetDumpSeverity() {
 #if defined(OFFICIAL_BUILD)
   return DCHECK_IS_ON() ? LOGGING_DCHECK : LOGGING_ERROR;
+#elif !DCHECK_IS_ON()
+  // Stedding: its releases are optimised builds that are not official ones
+  // (tooling/args/release.gn), and upstream stops the browser on these
+  // checks outside official builds, so a check that Chrome only reports
+  // stopped Stedding for the people using it. A build without DCHECKs is the
+  // one people run: it logs and writes a dump without crashing, as Chrome
+  // does. A build with DCHECKs, which the checks suites run on, still stops
+  // (docs/decisions/0024-soft-checks-report-in-releases.md).
+  return LOGGING_ERROR;
 #else
   // Crash outside official builds (outside user-facing builds) to detect
   // invariant violations early in release-build testing like fuzzing, etc.
